# docs.coti.io version pin

When writing or changing **docs.coti.io** pages for `@coti-io/coti-wallet-plugin` (integration guide, API, configuration, example app, AES onboarding, etc.):

1. Read the version from this repo’s `package.json` (the release being discussed).
2. State that version **on the page**, near the top (overview, prerequisites, or a “Applies to” line).
3. If the page covers a **future / unreleased** API, say so and still name the target version (e.g. “unreleased; intended for 0.4.0”).
4. Do not describe APIs as current without a version. Docs.coti.io outlives a single chat; readers must know which npm release the names and examples match.

```markdown
Applies to `@coti-io/coti-wallet-plugin@0.3.10`.
```

In-repo `README.md` may link to docs.coti.io; it does not replace pinning the version **on the docs.coti.io page itself**.
